{
  "id": "ingroup-bias",
  "term": "ingroup bias",
  "definition": "Ingroup bias is the tendency to favor one’s own group when responding or making judgments in social situations. The packet indicates that this tendency is usually stronger when a person identifies more strongly with the group and weaker when their group loyalty is less central.",
